# shell-team: this .gitignore is self-contained to the shell-team base dir,
# so the host repo's root .gitignore is never touched. Operating-Loop telemetry
# is regenerated each run and is not meant to be committed.
runs/
# codex-capture.sh per-invocation temps — a SIGKILL-orphaned temp can
# hold raw Codex output with PII; the trap-based cleanup doesn't fire on
# SIGKILL, so this pattern is the mandatory backstop (both-layout coverage).
reviews/.codex-capture.*
# codex-capture.sh --publish raw review captures. Raw Codex output can carry
# personal information, which is exactly why the pre-publish temps above are
# already ignored — a published <stem>.txt/.jsonl is the same raw content
# under its permanent name. The curated <task-id>.md review record a human
# writes from that raw output stays trackable (not matched by these three
# patterns); reviews/*.json is included defensively even though nothing ships
# that extension today.
reviews/*.txt
reviews/*.jsonl
reviews/*.json
